// wp_tick_step — one tick: sleep out the SLA period, then post a tick message
// to the disk controller's queue.
//
// AXVERITY_EXTENT_WRITE_PATH step 2. This thread NEVER touches a block, a
// pointer, or the store. It posts a message and goes back to sleep. All
// coalescing and all durability decisions happen in the disk controller and
// below — the timer and the flusher never talk to each other, and neither
// knows the other exists.
//
// UNIT BOUNDARY, stated because it already bit once. The knob is in
// MICROSECONDS, because that is what slab_open takes (`sla_us`). The bridge's
// `sleep` primitive is in MILLISECONDS (runtime/process.rs: `from_millis`) —
// `proc_sleep` is the seconds one. So the division happens here, at the single
// point where the two units meet, and nowhere else.
//
// A period under 1 ms would divide to a 0 ms sleep and turn this thread into a
// busy spin that starves the very pipeline it is timing, so it is refused
// loudly rather than floored. Sub-millisecond SLAs are not a tick's job.
//
// Sleeping BEFORE the send, not after, so a run that ends immediately does not
// post a spurious tick into a queue nobody will drain. The cost of that choice
// is that a finished run lingers up to one period while this thread sleeps out
// its last interval — bounded by the SLA, and the reason the run cell is
// checked on wake rather than being waited on.
//
// The message is [0]: kind 0 = tick. A write bundle is [1, <bundle>]. Kind
// leads so the disk controller can dispatch on list_get(msg, 0) without
// unpacking anything else — a write bundle travels nested and UNCHANGED, so
// flusher's message shape is untouched by this.
fn wp_tick_step(state: Text) -> Text {
  let us   = wp_tick_sla_us(Unit())
  let ms   = int_div(us, Int(1000))
  let _chk = if int_lt(ms, Int(1)) {
               let _m = io_println(str_concat(Text("FATAL sla_us_below_one_millisecond="),
                          str_concat(int_to_str(us),
                            Text(" — a sub-millisecond tick divides to a 0 ms sleep and busy-spins"))))
               proc_exit(Int(1))
             } else {
               io_print(Text(""))
             }
  let _s   = sleep(ms)
  let _p   = bchan_send(Text("wp-dc"), list_of_1(Int(0)))
  str_concat(state, Text(""))
}
